ion).\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education, 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere with crew. Strengths: reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere. Concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to develop.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership. Strengths: adaptability, concentration, problem solving, responsibility. Concerns: arrogance, weak leadership.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Likely Candidate B has strong reliability and stress, but uncooperative may be big issue. Candidate C is reliable, good decisions, positive crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may affect cooperation. Candidate D strong problem solving, responsibility, but arrogance and weak leadership. Candidate A strong anticipation and leadership but unorganized and poor at criticism.\n\nWhich is best? Probably Candidate C: reliability, decision quality, positive crew atmosphere outweigh communication difficulty? But communication is crucial. Candidate B's uncooperative is also serious. Candidate D's arrogance may affect crew. Candidate A's unorganized may affect reliability.\n\nThus I might recommend Candidate C, but note concerns.\n\nWe need to reference discussion: none yet, but we can say \"Given the facts we have, I propose...\"\n\nWe must include at least one fact as evidence. Provide two facts: 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, makes correct decisions quickly. Also note difficulty communicating.\n\nOk.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\"."}
